        {
          "id": 2459745721,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Or maybe `wsutil/epochs.h` should have macros that convert times using the other epoch into `time_t` values, so people don't have to remember whether to add or subtract the epoch offset, rather than macros that define the epoch offset? They should also do 64-bit arithmetic, to reduce the chances of overflows prior to assigning to a `time_t`.",
